WEBVTT

00:35:59.418 --> 00:36:01.745
AG: The other core value is learning.

00:36:01.769 --> 00:36:04.400
RS: We literally tell them
during the interview process,

00:36:04.424 --> 00:36:06.885
"If you don't know something, say it.

00:36:06.909 --> 00:36:08.990
It's okay to say, 'I don't know,' here.

00:36:09.014 --> 00:36:11.691
We don't want you to fake
knowledge that you don't have."

00:36:12.669 --> 00:36:15.735
AG: That's why they're willing
to audition people multiple times.

00:36:15.759 --> 00:36:16.933
It's a chance to gauge

00:36:16.957 --> 00:36:19.830
how much candidates have improved
their knowledge and skills.

00:36:19.854 --> 00:36:22.718
RS: So what I would say
is that what we're really looking for

00:36:22.742 --> 00:36:25.392
isn't deep expertise, but able learners.

00:36:26.528 --> 00:36:29.819
AG: I think it's time to base
hiring decisions less on credentials

00:36:29.843 --> 00:36:32.676
and more on the motivation
and ability to learn,